File: ToricVectorBundles.info, Node: areIsomorphic, Next: base, Prev: addFiltration, Up: Top

areIsomorphic -- checks if two vector bundles are isomorphic
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = areIsomorphic(E,F)
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
      * F, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether E and F are
        isomorphic

Description
===========


E and F must be vector bundles over the same fan and the filtrations must be
defined over the same ring. Two equivariant vector bundles in Klyachko's
description are isomorphic if there exists a simultaneous isomorphism for the
filtered vector spaces of all rays. The method then returns whether the bundles
are isomorphic.
+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : HF = hirzebruchFan 2                    |
|                                             |
|o1 = HF                                      |
|                                             |
|o1 : Fan                                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = exteriorPower(2, cotangentBundle HF)|
|                                             |
|o2 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }        |
|      number of affine charts => 4           |
|      number of rays => 4                    |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 1         |
|                                             |
|o2 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko               |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = weilToCartier({-1,-1,-1,-1},HF)     |
|                                             |
|o3 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }        |
|      number of affine charts => 4           |
|      number of rays => 4                    |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 1         |
|                                             |
|o3 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko               |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : areIsomorphic(E,F)                      |
|                                             |
|o4 = true                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+


To obtain the isomorphism, if two bundles are isomorphic use *note
isomorphism(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,ToricVectorBundleKlyachko):
isomorphism_lpToricVectorBundleKlyachko_cmToricVectorBundleKlyachko_rp,.

Caveat
======

If E and F are defined over different rings (e.g. QQ and ZZ) then
areIsomorphic(E,F) will return false. Likewise, if the bundles are only defined
over ZZ, the function will check for an isomorphism of the filtrations over ZZ.

See also
========

  * *note isomorphism(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,ToricVectorBundleKlyachko):
    isomorphism_lpToricVectorBundleKlyachko_cmToricVectorBundleKlyachko_rp, --
    the isomorphism if the two bundles are isomorphic
  * *note base: base, --  the basis matrices for the rays
  * *note filtration: filtration, --  the filtration matrices of the vector
    bundle
  * *note details: details, --  the details of a toric vector bundle

Ways to use areIsomorphic:
==========================

  * "areIsomorphic(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,ToricVectorBundleKlyachko)"

