cartierIndex --  the Cartier index of a Weil divisor
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = cartierIndex(L,F)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * F, an instance of the type *note Fan: (Polyhedra)Fan,, a pure and full
        dimensional fan
  * Outputs:
      * N, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,

Description
===========


L must be a list of weights, exactly one for each ray of the fan. Then the
Cartier index is the smallest strictly positive natural number $N$ such that
$N$ times the Weil divisor is Cartier. If the Weil divisor defined by these
weights is not *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,-Cartier, then $N$ would be infinity.
In this case cartierIndex returns an error. Otherwise it returns $N$.
+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : F = fan posHull matrix {{1,5},{5,1}}|
|                                         |
|o1 = F                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : Fan                                 |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = {2,2}                           |
|                                         |
|o2 = {2, 2}                              |
|                                         |
|o2 : List                                |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : cartierIndex(L,F)                   |
|                                         |
|o3 = 3                                   |
+-----------------------------------------+


If we change the Weil divisor we get a different Cartier index:
+----------------------+
|i4 : L = {3,3}        |
|                      |
|o4 = {3, 3}           |
|                      |
|o4 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i5 : cartierIndex(L,F)|
|                      |
|o5 = 2                |
+----------------------+

Caveat
======

The ordering of the list L must correspond to the ordering of the rays of the
fan output by *note raySortOfFan: raySortOfFan,.

See also
========

  * *note weilToCartier: weilToCartier, --  the line bundle given by a Cartier
    divisor

Ways to use cartierIndex:
=========================

  * "cartierIndex(List,Fan)"

