cokernel(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,Matrix) --  the cokernel of a morphism to a vector bundle
********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note cokernel: (Macaulay2Doc)cokernel,
  * Usage: 
        E1 = coker(E,M)
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, over *note ZZ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
  * Outputs:
      * E1, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,

Description
===========


M must be a matrix over *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note QQ:
(Macaulay2Doc)QQ, where the target space is the space of the bundle, i.e., the
matrix must have $k$ rows if the bundle has rank $k$. Then the new bundle is
given on each ray $\rho$ by the following filtration of coker(E,M)${}^\rho = (
E^{\rho} ) / $im(M) :


coker(E,M)${}^\rho(i) := E^{\rho}(i) / ( E^{\rho}(i) \cap $ im(M) ).
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : E = tangentBundle hirzebruchFan 2             |
|                                                   |
|o1 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }              |
|      number of affine charts => 4                 |
|      number of rays => 4                          |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 2               |
|                                                   |
|o1 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = E ** E                                    |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }              |
|      number of affine charts => 4                 |
|      number of rays => 4                          |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 4               |
|                                                   |
|o2 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = matrix {{1,0},{0,1},{1,0},{0,1/1}}        |
|                                                   |
|o3 = | 1 0 |                                       |
|     | 0 1 |                                       |
|     | 1 0 |                                       |
|     | 0 1 |                                       |
|                                                   |
|              4       2                            |
|o3 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : E1 = coker(E,M)                               |
|                                                   |
|o4 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }              |
|      number of affine charts => 4                 |
|      number of rays => 4                          |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 2               |
|                                                   |
|o4 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : details E1                                    |
|                                                   |
|o5 = HashTable{| -1 | => (| -1/2 1/2 |, | -2 -1 |)}|
|               | 2  |     | 1    0   |             |
|               | 0  | => (| 0 1 |, | -2 -1 |)      |
|               | -1 |     | 1 0 |                  |
|               | 0 | => (| 0 1 |, | -2 -1 |)       |
|               | 1 |     | 1 0 |                   |
|               | 1 | => (| 1 0 |, | -2 -1 |)       |
|               | 0 |     | 0 1 |                   |
|                                                   |
|o5 : HashTable                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note image(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,Matrix):
    image_lpToricVectorBundleKlyachko_cmMatrix_rp, --  the image of a vector
    bundle under a morphism
  * *note kernel(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,Matrix):
    kernel_lpToricVectorBundleKlyachko_cmMatrix_rp, --  the kernel of a
    morphism to a vector bundle

