filtration --  the filtration matrices of the vector bundle
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        f = filtration E
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,

Description
===========


For each ray of the fan there is a filtration matrix. If the bundle has rank
$k$ then this is a one row matrix over *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, with $k$
entries. This defines the filtration on the corresponding base matrix (see
*note base: base,) such that the $j$-th filtration is generated by all columns
of the base matrix for which the entry in the same column of the filtration
matrix is less or equal to $j$.
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : E = tangentBundle hirzebruchFan 2|
|                                      |
|o1 = {dimension of the variety => 2 } |
|      number of affine charts => 4    |
|      number of rays => 4             |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 2  |
|                                      |
|o1 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko        |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : filtration E                     |
|                                      |
|o2 = HashTable{| -1 | => | -1 0 |}    |
|               | 2  |                 |
|               | 0  | => | -1 0 |     |
|               | -1 |                 |
|               | 0 | => | -1 0 |      |
|               | 1 |                  |
|               | 1 | => | -1 0 |      |
|               | 0 |                  |
|                                      |
|o2 : HashTable                        |
+--------------------------------------+


So in this example for each ray the first column of the basis appears at -1 and
the second at 0.

See also
========

  * *note addFiltration: addFiltration, -- changing the filtration matrices of
    a toric vector bundle in Klyachko's description
  * *note base: base, --  the basis matrices for the rays
  * *note isVectorBundle: isVectorBundle, --  checks if the data does in fact
    define an equivariant toric vector bundle

Ways to use filtration:
=======================

  * "filtration(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note filtration: filtration, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

