isomorphism(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,ToricVectorBundleKlyachko) --  the isomorphism if the two bundles are isomorphic
**********************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isomorphism: (Isomorphism)isomorphism,
  * Usage: 
        M = isomorphism(E,F)
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
      * F, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Homogeneous: (Isomorphism)isomorphism, => ..., default value
        true,
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Strict: (Isomorphism)isomorphism, => ..., default value false, 
      * *note Tries: (Isomorphism)isomorphism, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Verbose: (Isomorphism)isomorphism, => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, over the ring over which the
        two bundles are defined

Description
===========


Two equivariant vector bundles in Klyachko's description are isomorphic if
there exists a simultaneous isomorphism for the filtered vector spaces of all
rays. If the two bundles are isomorphic (see *note areIsomorphic:
areIsomorphic,) this function returns the isomorphism. For this, the two
bundles must be defined over the same fan.
+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : HF = hirzebruchFan 2                    |
|                                             |
|o1 = HF                                      |
|                                             |
|o1 : Fan                                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = exteriorPower(2, cotangentBundle HF)|
|                                             |
|o2 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }        |
|      number of affine charts => 4           |
|      number of rays => 4                    |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 1         |
|                                             |
|o2 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko               |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = weilToCartier({-1,-1,-1,-1},HF)     |
|                                             |
|o3 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }        |
|      number of affine charts => 4           |
|      number of rays => 4                    |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 1         |
|                                             |
|o3 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko               |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = isomorphism(E,F)                    |
|                                             |
|o4 = | 1 |                                   |
|                                             |
|              1       1                      |
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                       |
+---------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note areIsomorphic: areIsomorphic, -- checks if two vector bundles are
    isomorphic
  * *note base: base, --  the basis matrices for the rays
  * *note filtration: filtration, --  the filtration matrices of the vector
    bundle
  * *note details: details, --  the details of a toric vector bundle

