twist --  twists a toric vector bundle with a line bundle
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        E1 = twist(E,L)
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
  * Outputs:
      * E1, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,

Description
===========


twist takes a toric vector bundle $E$ in Klyachko's description and a list of
integers L. The list must contain one entry for each ray of the underlying fan.
Then it computes the twist of the vector bundle by the line bundle given by
these integers (see *note weilToCartier: weilToCartier,).
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : E = tangentBundle hirzebruchFan 2           |
|                                                 |
|o1 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }            |
|      number of affine charts => 4               |
|      number of rays => 4                        |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 2             |
|                                                 |
|o1 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko                   |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = {1,-2,3,-4}                             |
|                                                 |
|o2 = {1, -2, 3, -4}                              |
|                                                 |
|o2 : List                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E1 = twist(E,L)                             |
|                                                 |
|o3 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }            |
|      number of affine charts => 4               |
|      number of rays => 4                        |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 2             |
|                                                 |
|o3 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko                   |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : details E1                                  |
|                                                 |
|o4 = HashTable{| -1 | => (| -1 1/2 |, | -4 -3 |)}|
|               | 2  |     | 2  0   |             |
|               | 0  | => (| 0  1 |, | -2 -1 |)   |
|               | -1 |     | -1 0 |               |
|               | 0 | => (| 0 1 |, | 1 2 |)       |
|               | 1 |     | 1 0 |                 |
|               | 1 | => (| 1 0 |, | 3 4 |)       |
|               | 0 |     | 0 1 |                 |
|                                                 |
|o4 : HashTable                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The ordering of the list L must correspond to the ordering of the rays of the
fan output by *note raySortOfFan: raySortOfFan,.

